---
import EyebrowLabel from "../ui/EyebrowLabel.astro";
---

<section class="section" id="ai">
  <div class="ai__inner">
    <EyebrowLabel>AI-Native by Design</EyebrowLabel>
    <h2 class="section-title ai__h2">
      The first loyalty platform built around the Model Context Protocol.
    </h2>
    <div class="ai__body">
      <p class="section-body">
        Most loyalty platforms bolt on AI as an afterthought. LoyaltyOS started
        the other way around: the program is exposed as MCP tools first, and the
        UI is built on top of the same surface your agents already use. Claude,
        ChatGPT, Cursor, or any MCP-compatible agent can run your loyalty
        program end to end — no scraping, no brittle integrations.
      </p>
      <p class="section-body">
        The AI layer ships in three pieces: a self-hostable MCP server, a Cowork
        skill with pre-built loyalty workflows, and an in-admin companion
        powered by OpenRouter so you can pick any model you prefer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ai__cards">
      <div class="ai-card">
        <span class="ai-card__path">apps/mcp-server · ghcr.io/jvillatox/loyaltyos-mcp:1.1.0</span>
        <h3 class="ai-card__title">MCP server</h3>
        <p class="ai-card__body">
          ~22 tools across members, campaigns, segments, analytics, coupons,
          rewards, and coalition. Dual transport: stdio for local agents (Claude
          Code, Cursor) and HTTP/SSE for remote agents. Auth via API key
          forwarded to the existing Fastify API — the MCP server never touches
          your database directly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="ai-card">
        <span class="ai-card__path">packages/ai/skill/</span>
        <h3 class="ai-card__title">Cowork skill: loyaltyos-assistant</h3>
        <p class="ai-card__body">
          Five pre-built workflows wired to the MCP tools, including: program
          health check, inactive-member reactivation, single-member
          investigation, targeted segment build, and coalition reconciliation
          report. Drop the skill into any Cowork session — it knows your domain.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="ai-card">
        <span class="ai-card__path">packages/ai/companion + apps/admin</span>
        <h3 class="ai-card__title">Admin companion</h3>
        <p class="ai-card__body">
          A slide-over chat panel inside the admin UI. OpenRouter under the
          hood, so you swap between Claude, GPT-4o, Gemini, or any supported
          model with one config change. Two modes: read-only for instant
          questions, and action mode with a confirmation preview before any
          mutation runs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ai__prompt-block">
      <span class="ai__prompt-label">Example prompt</span>
      <pre class="ai__prompt-text"><code>"Create a reactivation campaign for members inactive 90+ days with a 2× points coupon valid for 14 days. Show me the preview first."</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="ai__prompt-caption">
      One sentence runs segment_query → coupon_create → campaign_create →
      campaign_trigger, with a preview step you confirm before anything writes.
    </p>

    <p class="ai__footnote">
      The MCP server is merged. The skill and companion are landing in v1.1. The
      platform itself does not require any AI — the core works without an LLM
      key.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ai__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .ai__h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 792px;
  }

  .ai__body {
    max-width: 588px;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .ai__cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .ai__cards {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .ai-card {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--card-pad-desk);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .ai-card__path {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .ai-card__title {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .ai-card__body {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai__prompt-block {
    background: var(--code-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .ai__prompt-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .ai__prompt-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .ai__prompt-caption {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    max-width: 588px;
  }

  .ai__footnote {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    max-width: 588px;
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
</style>
